			<item>
				<title>Real-Time Aggregations with Kafka Streams at 10K Events/Sec</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/real-time-aggregations-with-kafka-streams-at-10k-events-sec/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:14:20 +0530</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/real-time-aggregations-with-kafka-streams-at-10k-events-sec/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part 3 of the StreamMetrics Series&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;*Previous parts: &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-a-production-kafka-producer/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 1: Kafka Producer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-production-grade-kafka-consumer-patterns/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 2: Consumer + DLQ&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | *&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/from-localhost-to-kubernetes-deploying-streammetrics-at-scale/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 4: From Localhost to Kubernetes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Building production-grade streaming analytics: windows, state stores, and performance validation&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Parts 1 and 2, we built a Kafka producer and consumer that process individual events reliably. But processing 10,000 raw events per second creates a new problem:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How do you extract insights from that fire hose of data?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>From Localhost to Kubernetes: Deploying StreamMetrics at Scale</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/from-localhost-to-kubernetes-deploying-streammetrics-at-scale/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:14:19 +0530</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/from-localhost-to-kubernetes-deploying-streammetrics-at-scale/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part 4 of the StreamMetrics Series&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;*Previous parts: &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-a-production-kafka-producer/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 1: Kafka Producer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-production-grade-kafka-consumer-patterns/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 2: Consumer + DLQ&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | *&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/real-time-aggregations-with-kafka-streams-at-10k-events-sec/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 3: Real-Time Aggregations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Streammetric Bottleneck Explainer by NotebookLM&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/embed/2Bs8K6folk0?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Love how after building something locally, you think &amp;ldquo;&lt;em&gt;okay, it works on my machine!&lt;/em&gt;&amp;rdquo; and then reality hits when you try to deploy it. Docker says &amp;ldquo;&lt;em&gt;works on my machine&lt;/em&gt;&amp;rdquo; is not an excuse anymore, and Kubernetes says &amp;ldquo;&lt;em&gt;hold my beer, let&amp;rsquo;s make it production-ready.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Production Monitoring: You Can&#39;t Fix What You Can&#39;t See</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/production-monitoring-you-can-t-fix-what-you-can-t-see/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:14:19 +0530</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/production-monitoring-you-can-t-fix-what-you-can-t-see/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Previous parts: &#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-a-production-kafka-producer/&#34;&gt;Part 1: Kafka Producer&lt;/a&gt; | &#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-production-grade-kafka-consumer-patterns/&#34;&gt;Part 2: Consumer + DLQ&lt;/a&gt; | &#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/real-time-aggregations-with-kafka-streams-at-10k-events-sec/&#34;&gt;Part 3: Real-Time Aggregations&lt;/a&gt; | &#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/from-localhost-to-kubernetes-deploying-streammetrics-at-scale/&#34;&gt;Part 4: Docker + Kubernetes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You know that feeling when your app is running in production and someone asks &amp;ldquo;Is everything okay?&amp;rdquo; and you respond with &amp;ldquo;&amp;hellip;I think so?&amp;rdquo; Yeah, that&amp;rsquo;s not good enough.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;After deploying StreamMetrics to Kubernetes with a 3-node KRaft Kafka cluster, dockerized microservices, and validated 10K events/sec throughput, I realized I was flying blind. Sure, the pods were running. The logs looked fine. But I had no idea:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Building Production-Grade Apache Kafka Consumer Patterns</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-production-grade-kafka-consumer-patterns/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:14:15 +0530</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-production-grade-kafka-consumer-patterns/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part 2 of the StreamMetrics Series&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;*Previous parts: &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-a-production-kafka-producer/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 1: Kafka Producer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | &lt;em&gt;&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/real-time-aggregations-with-kafka-streams-at-10k-events-sec/&#34;&gt;*Part 3: Real-time Aggregation *&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt; | *&#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/from-localhost-to-kubernetes-deploying-streammetrics-at-scale/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part 4: From Localhost to Kubernetes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A deep-dive into manual offset management, dead letter queues, and observability with Spring Boot + Apache Kafka. This is part 2 of the series Stream Metrics application. *In &#xA;      &#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/dynamicallyblunttech/posts/building-a-production-kafka-producer/&#34;&gt;Part 1&lt;/a&gt; we built the producer, today we add the consumer.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;why-this-matters&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Matters&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#why-this-matters&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most tutorials show you how to build a Kafka consumer. They show you @KafkaListener, they show you how to read a message, and they call it production-ready. It is not!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
